IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tma-types`

-- Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK) — GOAL 2: PAYMENT (ss 59A, 59B).
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1970-9.txt.

§ `Goal 2 — payment`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

-- s 59A(1): payments on account apply if, for the preceding year, the
-- assessed amount exceeds tax deducted at source, the excess ("the relevant
-- amount") is not less than the prescribed amount, and its proportion of the
-- assessed amount is not less than the prescribed proportion.
@ref s 59A(1)
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the relevant amount for` p MEANS
    p's `previous year's assessed amount` MINUS p's `previous year's tax deducted at source`

@ref s 59A(1)
@export Whether payments on account of income tax are due under s 59A of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): for the preceding year the self-assessed amount exceeded tax deducted at source by a relevant amount not less than the prescribed minimum, and that amount is not less than the prescribed proportion of the assessed amount. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`  @desc The preceding year's assessed amount and tax deducted at source, and the prescribed minimum amount and proportion
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `payments on account are due under` p IF
        `the relevant amount for` p GREATER THAN 0
    AND `the relevant amount for` p AT LEAST p's `prescribed minimum relevant amount`
    AND `the relevant amount for` p AT LEAST p's `prescribed minimum proportion` TIMES p's `previous year's assessed amount`

-- s 59A(2) "two payments on account ... (a) the first on or before the 31st
-- January in that year, and (b) the second on or before the next following
-- 31st July; and ... each ... of an amount equal to 50 per cent. of the
-- relevant amount."
@ref s 59A(2)
@export Each payment on account under s 59A(2) of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): 50% of the relevant amount, or 0 if payments on account are not due. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`  @desc The preceding year's figures and the prescribed thresholds
GIVETH A NUMBER
`each payment on account under` p MEANS
    IF `payments on account are due under` p THEN `the relevant amount for` p TIMES 0.5 ELSE 0

@ref s 59A(2)(a)
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the first payment on account date for` p MEANS Date 31 1 (p's `tax year` PLUS 1)

@ref s 59A(2)(b)
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`
GIVETH A DATE
`the second payment on account date for` p MEANS Date 31 7 (p's `tax year` PLUS 1)

-- s 59B(1): the difference between the self-assessed tax and the payments on
-- account made and tax deducted at source is payable (or, if negative,
-- repayable).
@ref s 59B(1)
@export The balancing payment under s 59B(1) of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): the self-assessed income tax and capital gains tax for the year, less payments on account made and tax deducted at source; a negative amount is repayable. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`  @desc The self-assessed tax, payments on account made, and tax deducted at source
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the balancing payment under` p MEANS
    p's `self-assessed tax` MINUS p's `payments on account made` MINUS p's `tax deducted at source`

-- s 59B(3) "In a case where the person— (a) gave the notice required by
-- section 7 ... within six months from the end of the year of assessment,
-- but (b) was not given notice under section 8 ... until after the 31st
-- October next following that year, the difference shall be payable ... at
-- the end of the period of three months beginning with the day on which the
-- notice under section 8 ... was given." (4) "In any other case ... on or
-- before the 31st January next following the year of assessment."
@ref s 59B(3)-(4)
@export The due date of the balancing payment under s 59B of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK): 31 January after the tax year, or, for a person who notified chargeability within six months but was given notice to file only after 31 October, the end of the three months beginning with that notice. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Payment facts`  @desc The tax year, whether chargeability was notified in time, and the date of the notice to file
GIVETH A DATE
`the balancing payment date for` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `notice to file given on`
    WHEN JUST n THEN
        IF   p's `notified chargeability in time` AND n GREATER THAN Date 31 10 (p's `tax year` PLUS 1)
        THEN `the last day of the` 3 `months beginning with` n
        ELSE Date 31 1 (p's `tax year` PLUS 2)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN Date 31 1 (p's `tax year` PLUS 2)

-- s 59B(6) tax under another assessment is "payable on the day following the
-- end of the period of 30 days beginning with the day on which the notice of
-- assessment is given" — the notice date + 30.
@ref s 59B(6)
@export The due date under s 59B(6) of the Taxes Management Act 1970 (UK) for tax payable under an assessment other than a self-assessment: the day after the end of the 30 days beginning with the day the notice of assessment is given (that day + 30). DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN n IS A DATE  @desc The day the notice of assessment was given
GIVETH A DATE
`the due date for an assessment notified on` n MEANS
    Date (Day n PLUS 30)
